## 8. On-device op plan (Sprite llama.cpp fork, Hexagon v79)

**Ops that exist today [R, `ggml-hexagon.cpp` at native `292a145`]:**
- MUL_MAT for Q1_0, Q2_0, Q4_0 and Q8_0 (HMX for prefill).
- GATED_DELTA_NET (scalar and per-channel gate, so GDN now and KDA later) and SSM_CONV.
- FLASH_ATTN_EXT (F16/Q8 KV, masks, sinks).
- ROPE imrope; RMS/L2 norm; GLU; sigmoid; softmax; top-k; get/set_rows; concat; roll.
- Media rows enter through `llama_batch.embd`. Patchify, unpatchify and the Euler loop run on the host CPU, and the media projections are plain MUL_MAT.

**New or extended kernels**, in this order (each about 1 day plus qualification: simulator gate, phone numerics against CPU, whole-model parity, APK; precedent LUT and split-KV [R]):

| # | Kernel | Why | Fallback |
|---|---|---|---|
| K1 | **DEPTH_ATTN_RES**, fused HVX: norm, dot with the pseudo-query over at most 9 vectors, softmax, weighted sum | 48 (2B) or 64 (4B) calls per token; decomposed costs 2.8-7.5 ms | 5 existing ops per call |
| K2 | FLASH_ATTN_EXT split-KV for **head dim 256** and KV beyond 32,768 | Today it handles head 128 and KV up to 32k only; every 32k+ number above depends on it | non-split FA (the slower corner) |
| K3 | GDN state save/restore for the denoising loop (`llama_state_seq_get/set` or a `seq_cp` scratch sequence) | Every flow step must restart from the end-of-prefix state | host copy; UNVERIFIED on Hexagon |
| K4 | Reversed `get_rows` for the A8 span scan | Bidirectional media in the recurrent layers | host-side reverse |
| K5 | BLOCK_SPARSE_FA (block-mean scores, top-k, gathered FA) | Far-context decode beyond 32k | top_k + get_rows + FA; ships only if A3 passes |
| (K6) | Fix the multi-session GDN bug | Only needed if a config cannot fit one session | GDN on CPU [R] |

**Not used:** LIGHTNING_INDEXER, DSV4_HC_*, SSM_SCAN, MLA, MUL_MAT_ID.

**GGUF.** A new `chimera-omni` architecture extends `export/gguf_writer.py` `QWEN35_ARCH` with AttnRes tensors, the raw boundary and the raw head. Not built. Until it is, R9 stays partial.

