## 9. Initialisation and training

**Initialisation.**
- `co2-2b`: Qwen3.5-2B text trunk. Download it to Lexar (317 GB free; the AI share is full). Its ViT is discarded.
- `co2-4b`: Qwen3.5-4B text trunk (on disk), or the best OC01 4B fold child (X00/X31, 10-15/15). Choose with A0b.
- Fallback for the 2B: fold 4B to 2B.
- New tensors start function-preserving:
  - AttnRes queries at zero.
  - Bridge and head random. They touch only media rows, so text is exactly the parent's at step 0 (A0 gate).
  - Control rows at the mean of the text embeddings.
- The 0.8B import plus qwen35 GGUF round-trip is already proven [R: `CO/receipts/qwen35_0p8b_*`].

**Hardware reality and the critique fixes.**
- The training lane is P40 fp32. SM61 has no bf16, Triton does not run (`streamed_kd_trainer.py:333` [R]), and the training venv's torch cu128 has no SM61 kernels, so P40 runs use a cu124/cu126 torch.
- A 2B with fp32 Adam needs about 31 GB against 24 GB per card [V arithmetic: 1.92e9 x 16 B]. Use a host-offloaded optimizer state (the streamed engine) or a factored optimizer.
- Mandatory:
  - Chunked lm_head and chunked CE/top-k-KL (one 64k x 248,832 fp32 logit tensor is 65 GB).
  - `--sdpa-gqa repeat`.
  - The memory-efficient attention kernel with the explicit media mask.
  - P2P between P40s is broken, so transfers go through the host [R].
- The "86M tok/day for the 2B" is **UNVERIFIED**. Re-measure it on a 0.8B P40 cell before sizing any stage.
- The linear layers train as **GDN** using the existing torch chunk rule (scalar decay). The repo's `KimiDeltaAttention` forward is a per-position Python loop, which is fine for the proxy and useless at 4k+ (critique 1). Building a P40-capable chunked GDN/KDA in torch is training-engine work item T1.
- The training engine must run the Chimera layout with media rows. Today's measured engines are Qwen3_5 text-only (review §7, root cause 5). This is the biggest item, T2.

**Stages.** Each stage is an omni_lab run. Grading is behaviour-first on frozen evals and never gates on token match.

